      "problem": "The product of any two integers is divisible by those two integers.\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The word \"any\" indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $∀.$\n\n- The sentence refers to two integers. So, by denoting our numbers as $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n∀\\,a,b\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n(a∣ab)\\,∧\\,(b∣ab)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$∀a,b\\in Z,\\,(a∣ab)\\,∧\\,(b∣ab)$",
